scriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2015-02-27T19:29:55Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/76493215","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/327#issuecomment-76493215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/327","id":76493215,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2NDkzMjE1","user":{"login":"jeoliva","id":7904247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDQyNDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7904247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva","html_url":"https://github.com/jeoliva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-27T23:37:58Z","updated_at":"2015-02-27T23:37:58Z","body":"@ojw28, in my humble opinion I don't think implementing remove_dot_segments is an urgent need. I don't know any CDN, media server or encoder that is producing HLS streams whose segments/media playlists/encryption urls are defined using \"../\" or \"./\" (much less using other character combinations like /../ or /./).\n\nAnd, as you said, in 99.9% of cases this is going to be supported directly by the web server receiving the requests. However, strictly speaking we should implement that also in the client/player side. The good point is we don't need to reinvent the wheel, this is a very known piece of code (that is even part of Android source code). See canonicalizePath method here: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/libcore/+/9b510df35b57946d843ffc34cf23fdcfc84c5220/luni/src/main/java/libcore/net/url/UrlUtils.java\n\nSo, given how easy this would be, my two cents go to adding this. Not something urgent, but a task for the future.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/76493215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jeoliva","id":7904247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDQyNDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7904247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva","html_url":"https://github.com/jeoliva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeoliva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":243640628,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MjQzNjQwNjI4","url":"https: